<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_n0006/tu_0012> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "• Low intensity interval training may be used at the initial stages of high risk HFrEF patients. The hard ( \\geq VT_1 or at 50% workload, RPE 11–12) and recovery ( <20 W) segments are usually 20–30 s and 40–60 s in duration. The primary aim should be to increase the duration from 15 to 30 min, with 2–3 sessions/week and 10–12 work phases per session" .
